('a37d721b-3834-4086-b12d-cf25e2e146c0','image',$c$This scooter weighs 67kg. The Kaabo Wolf King GTR Max has a 105 km/h top speed, a 200 km claimed range and a weight of more than four and a half Segway Ninebot E2 Plus scooters (14.4kg each). It is a private land scooter in every state and territory. Weight is the spec nobody puts on the box. Compare weight, range and price for every scooter at scootfinder.au. What is the heaviest thing you have carried up stairs?$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/8d22722/posts/2026-10-12/scootfinder/p01-mon-am-wolf-king-67kg.jpg'],'2026-10-11T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','sf-2026-10-12-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 11 Oct: full size eye audit of every slide/frame, live feed dupe check (2 reels live), facts per manifest sources, white bg corners, no dashes. Hook: THIS SCOOTER WEIGHS 67KG.$a$),
('5649f5ce-3f06-4d07-83dc-1e02e66ad18c','image',$c$This scooter weighs 67kg.

That is the Kaabo Wolf King GTR Max: 105 km/h top speed, 200 km claimed range, dual motors and a weight of 67kg. A Segway Ninebot E2 Plus weighs 14.4kg, so you are carrying more than four and a half of them.

It is a private land scooter in every Australian state and territory, so the only stairs you will be negotiating are the ones at home. Weight is the spec nobody puts on the box cover.

Would you ever carry it? Tell us the heaviest thing you have hauled up a flight of stairs.

