('a37d721b-3834-4086-b12d-cf25e2e146c0','reel',$c$3 flights of stairs. Which scooter are you carrying? 15.6kg Inmotion Air, 18.1kg Xiaomi 6 Lite, 20.8kg Inmotion Climber, 30kg iScooter iX7 Pro, 53.1kg Segway GT3 Pro. Weights are manufacturer listed figures from scootfinder.au, not a physical carry test. Compare weight, range and price for every scooter at scootfinder.au. What is your carry limit?$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/8d22722/posts/2026-10-12/scootfinder/p04-tue-pm-carry-test-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-13T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','sf-2026-10-13-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 11 Oct: full size eye audit of every slide/frame, live feed dupe check (2 reels live), facts per manifest sources, white bg corners, no dashes. Hook: 3 FLIGHTS OF STAIRS. WHICH SCOOTER ARE YOU CARRYING?$a$),
('5649f5ce-3f06-4d07-83dc-1e02e66ad18c','reel',$c$3 flights of stairs. Which scooter are you carrying?

15.6kg Inmotion Air: one hand. 18.1kg Xiaomi 6 Lite: still fine. 20.8kg Inmotion Climber: arm check. 30kg iScooter iX7 Pro: ask for help. 53.1kg Segway GT3 Pro: call a mover.

These are manufacturer listed weights from our directory, not a physical carry test. But weight is the spec nobody puts on the box, and it decides whether you actually use the thing.

What is your carry limit? Tell us below.

