('a37d721b-3834-4086-b12d-cf25e2e146c0','image',$c$Off road. Not off puddles. The iScooter iX7 Pro has an IPX4 rating, which means water splashed from any direction. IPX5 is water jets, IPX6 is heavy jets, IPX7 is a dunk in up to 1m. No e-scooter is truly waterproof. We list the IP rating on every scooter at scootfinder.au. Ever regretted a puddle?$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/8d22722/posts/2026-10-12/scootfinder/p06-wed-pm-ipx4-spec-check.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','sf-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 11 Oct: full size eye audit of every slide/frame, live feed dupe check (2 reels live), facts per manifest sources, white bg corners, no dashes. Hook: OFF ROAD. NOT OFF PUDDLES.$a$),
('5649f5ce-3f06-4d07-83dc-1e02e66ad18c','image',$c$Off road. Not off puddles.

The iScooter iX7 Pro is a dual motor off roader with 10 inch tubeless tyres. Its water rating is IPX4: water splashed from any direction. IPX5 is water jets, IPX6 is heavy jets and IPX7 is a dunk in up to 1m of water. IPX4 is not a puddle rating, and it is definitely not a hose rating.

We list the rating on every scooter at ScootFinder so you know what the number actually means before you ride home in the rain.

Have you ever ridden through a puddle and regretted it? Tell us below.

#escooter #scootfinder #speccheck #ipx4 #australia
